warning[and-or-precedence]: `state === nothing || values === nothing && return nothing` means `state === nothing || (values === nothing && return nothing)`
 --> positive.jl:3:5
  |
3 |     state === nothing || values === nothing && return nothing
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ parsed as `state === nothing || (values === nothing && return nothing)`
  |                          ------------------------------------ binds first
  |
  = why: `&&` binds tighter than `||`; read left to right, code looks like `(a || b) && c`
  = fix: replace with `(values === nothing && return nothing)`   [safe]
  = docs: corset explain and-or-precedence
  = note: warn from readability group, library preset
  = note: opt out with `# corset: allow and-or-precedence -- <reason>`

